      "q": "1. Describe the composition of the atmosphere.",
      "a": "wer:\nThe composition of the atmosphere is made up of gases, water vapour and dust particles. Gases include nitrogen (which is the most abundant), oxygen (essential for living beings), argon, carbon dioxide (important for the greenhouse effect), and ozone (which filters ultraviolet radiation).\nThe amount of carbon dioxide has been increasing due to burning of fossil fuels, affecting temperatures. Water vapour varies from 4% in humid tropics to less than 1% in dry polar regions, and it acts like a blanket, moderating temperature.\nDust particles, originating from sources like sea salts, soil, ash, pollen and meteors, are concentrated mainly in the lower atmosphere and play an important role in cloud formation by acting as nuclei for condensation."
