      "q": "2. Answer the following questions in about 30 words.\ni. Why do we call the earth a Blue Planet?",
      "a": "wer:\nThe Earth is called a Blue Planet because about 71% of its surface is covered with water, mainly in oceans, which makes it appear blue when viewed from space.\nii. What is a continental margin?\nAnswer:\nA continental margin refers to the zone of the ocean floor that separates the thin oceanic crust from thick continental crust, including the continental shelf, slope and rise.\niii. List out the deepest trenches of various oceans.\nAnswer:\nThe deepest trenches include: the Mariana Trench (Pacific Ocean), Puerto Rico Trench (Atlantic Ocean), Java Trench (Indian Ocean), and the Eurasian Basin (Arctic Ocean).\niv. What is a thermocline?\nAnswer:\nA thermocline is the layer in the ocean where the temperature decreases rapidly with increasing depth, usually found between the surface warm water and the deep cold water.\nv. When you move into the ocean what thermal layers would you encounter? Why the temperature varies with depth?\nAnswer:\nYou would encounter three layers: the surface warm layer, the thermocline (rapid temperature fall), and the deep cold layer. Temperature varies with depth due to sun\u2019s heat being absorbed at the surface and less light penetrating deeper.\nvi. What is salinity of sea water?\nAnswer:\nSalinity of sea water refers to the total amount of dissolved salts in sea water, usually measured as grams per 1,000 grams (or parts per thousand - \u2030)."
