      "q": "3. Answer the following questions in about 150 words.\ni. How are various elements of the hydrological cycle interrelated?",
      "a": "wer:\nThe hydrological cycle describes the continuous movement of water on, in, and above the Earth. Evaporation from oceans and land surfaces turns water into vapor, which rises and cools to form clouds (condensation).\nThese clouds result in precipitation (rain, snow). Part of the water is absorbed by the ground (infiltration) or returns to oceans via surface runoff and rivers. Ice and snow melt contribute to surface flow, while plant transpiration adds to atmospheric moisture.\nAll these processes are interdependent, ensuring the renewal and distribution of water across the planet and maintaining ecological balance.\nii. Examine the factors that influence the temperature distribution of the oceans.\nAnswer:\nFactors influencing ocean temperature distribution include: latitude (temperature decreases from equator to poles), unequal distribution of land and water (northern hemisphere oceans are warmer), prevailing winds (which can cause upwelling of cold water or pile up warm water), and ocean currents (warm or cold currents impact temperature).\nEnclosed seas in low latitudes tend to be warmer, while those in high latitudes are colder. Surface temperature is always highest because the sun\u2019s rays heat the upper layers, and temperature decreases with depth due to limited sunlight penetration.\nNCERT Chapter-wise Solutions: Water (Oceans) \u2013 Key Concepts\nThe\nWater (Oceans)\nchapter in NCERT Geography deepens your understanding of the\nhydrological cycle, ocean relief, temperature, and salinity\n. Mastering these fundamentals is crucial for building a strong base in Geography and performing well in exams.\nRegular practice of\nchapter-wise NCERT solutions\nhelps clarify complex topics like ocean currents, submarine features, and water composition. Focusing on these high-weightage concepts ensures better retention and boosts confidence for competitive exams.\nFor effective exam prep, revise\nimportant diagrams, tables, and flowcharts\nfrom the Water (Oceans) NCERT chapter. Apply concise answers, key terms, and examples to increase your accuracy and maximize marks in Geography assessments.\nCBSE Class 11 Geography Chapter-wise NCERT Solutions\nS.No\nChapter-wise NCERT Solutions for Geography Class 11\n1\nChapter 1 - Geography as a Discipline Solutions\n2\nChapter 2 - The Origin and Evolution of the Earth Solutions\n3\nChapter 3 - Interior of the Earth Solutions\n4\nChapter 4 - Distribution of Oceans and Continents Solutions\n5\nChapter 5 - Geomorphic Processes Solutions\n6\nChapter 6 - Landforms and Their Evolution Solutions\n7\nChapter 7 - Composition and Structure of Atmosphere Solutions\n8\nChapter 8 - Solar Radiation Heat Balance and Temperature Solutions\n9\nChapter 9 - Atmospheric Circulation and Weather Systems Solutions\n10\nChapter 10 - Water in the Atmosphere Solutions\n11\nChapter 11 - World Climate and Climate Change Solutions\n12\nChapter 13 - Movements of Ocean Water Solutions\n13\nChapter 14 - Biodiversity and Conservation Solutions\nCBSE Class 11 Geography Study Materials\nS.No\nStudy Materials for Class 11 Geography\n1\nCBSE Class 11 Geography NCERT Solutions\n2\nCBSE Class 11 Geography NCERT Book"
