      "q": "2. Answer the following questions in about 30 words.\ni. What are waves?",
      "a": "wer:\nWaves are the energy that moves across the ocean surface. They appear as the rise and fall of water, but the water particles themselves move in small circles as the wave passes, transferring energy rather than the actual water.\nii. Where do waves in the ocean get their energy from?\nAnswer:\nWaves in the ocean get their energy primarily from the wind. As wind blows over the water's surface, it transfers energy to the water, creating waves that travel across the ocean.\niii. What are tides?\nAnswer:\nTides are the periodical rise and fall of sea level once or twice daily. They are mainly caused by the gravitational pull of the moon and, to a lesser extent, the sun on the earth\u2019s oceans.\niv. How are tides caused?\nAnswer:\nTides are caused by the gravitational attraction of the moon and the sun and the centrifugal force created by the rotation of the earth-moon system. This leads to the regular rise and fall of sea levels.\nv. How are tides related to navigation?\nAnswer:\nTides play an important role in navigation. Knowledge of tidal heights is crucial for ships entering and leaving harbours, especially those near river estuaries. High tides help ships to safely cross shallow bars."
