      "q": "3. Answer the following questions in about 150 words.\ni. How do currents affect the temperature? How does it affect the temperature of coastal areas in the N. W. Europe?",
      "a": "wer:\nOcean currents, by moving large volumes of water, transport heat from one part of the world to another. Warm currents raise the temperature of coastal areas, while cold currents lower it.\nFor example, the North Atlantic Drift (a warm current) flows along the northwest coast of Europe. This warms the coastal regions of countries like the United Kingdom and Ireland, making their climates much milder than other places at similar latitudes.\nAs a result, these areas experience cool summers and mild winters, with a moderate temperature range. Conversely, cold currents lower the average temperature where they flow past a coast. Thus, ocean currents significantly influence the climate and temperature of coastal regions around the world.\nii. What are the causes of currents?\nAnswer:\nOcean currents are caused by various factors. The primary causes include the heating by solar energy, which creates temperature differences and water expansion; wind, which imparts energy to the water\u2019s surface; gravity, which pulls water down slopes created by temperature and salinity differences; and the coriolis force, which deflects the path of moving water due to Earth's rotation.\nSecondary factors include variations in salinity and density, which cause vertical movement, and the shape of the ocean basins and coastlines, which determine the directions of the currents. Prevailing winds and the position of the continents also play significant roles in the formation and direction of ocean currents.\nUnderstanding Movements of Ocean Water\nThe chapter on\nMovements of Ocean Water\nexplores the fascinating phenomena of waves, tides, and ocean currents. Learning these fundamental processes helps students understand how the ocean shapes Earth\u2019s climate and influences human activity across the globe.\nGrasping the details of\nwaves, tides, and currents\nwill make concepts clearer and boost your exam preparation. Focus on differences between these movements and remember key examples like the North Atlantic Drift for thorough revision.\nRegularly practicing\nNCERT-based questions\nwill help reinforce your understanding. Revising these chapters will enhance conceptual clarity, helping you score better in Geography for the 2026-27 board exams and beyond.\nCBSE Class 11 Geography Chapter-wise NCERT Solutions\nS.No\nChapter-wise NCERT Solutions for Geography Class 11\n1\nChapter 1 - Geography as a Discipline Solutions\n2\nChapter 2 - The Origin and Evolution of the Earth Solutions\n3\nChapter 3 - Interior of the Earth Solutions\n4\nChapter 4 - Distribution of Oceans and Continents Solutions\n5\nChapter 5 - Geomorphic Processes Solutions\n6\nChapter 6 - Landforms and Their Evolution Solutions\n7\nChapter 7 - Composition and Structure of Atmosphere Solutions\n8\nChapter 8 - Solar Radiation Heat Balance and Temperature Solutions\n9\nChapter 9 - Atmospheric Circulation and Weather Systems Solutions\n10\nChapter 10 - Water in the Atmosphere Solutions\n11\nChapter 11 - World Climate and Climate Change Solutions\n12\nChapter 12 - Water Oceans Solutions\n13\nChapter 14 - Biodiversity and Conservation Solutions\nCBSE Class 11 Geography Study Materials\nS.No\nStudy Materials for Class 11 Geography\n1\nCBSE Class 11 Geography NCERT Solutions\n2\nCBSE Class 11 Geography NCERT Book"
