      "q": "2. Answer the following questions in about 30 words.\n(i) What is biodiversity?",
      "a": "wer:\nBiodiversity is the number and variety of organisms found within a specified geographic region. It includes the varieties of plants, animals and micro-organisms, their genes, and the ecosystems they form, representing the variability among living organisms on earth.\n(ii) What are the different levels of biodiversity?\nAnswer:\nThe three levels of biodiversity are: (1) Genetic diversity \u2013 variation of genes within species, (2) Species diversity \u2013 variety and number of species in a defined area, and (3) Ecosystem diversity \u2013 diversity of habitats and ecological processes in different ecosystem types.\n(iii) What do you understand by \u2018hotspots\u2019?\nAnswer:\nHotspots are areas that are rich in species diversity, especially those with high levels of endemic species. These areas are identified for concentrated conservation efforts as they are most vulnerable and important for biodiversity conservation.\n(iv) Discuss briefly the importance of animals to human kind.\nAnswer:\nAnimals play crucial roles in ecological balance by pollinating plants, decomposing organic materials, cycling nutrients, serving as food and resources, and maintaining overall ecosystem health. They contribute greatly to the survival and development of human society.\n(v) What do you understand by \u2018exotic species\u2019?\nAnswer:\nExotic species are species which are not native to a particular habitat but have been introduced into it. These species can sometimes cause extensive damage to the local ecosystem and its native biotic community."
