      "q": "3. Answer the following questions in about 150 words.\n(i) What are the roles played by biodiversity in the shaping of nature?",
      "a": "wer:\nBiodiversity plays multiple roles in shaping nature through its ecological, economic, and scientific influence.\nEcologically, diverse species capture and store energy, cycle water and nutrients, and help to fix atmospheric gases, all of which sustain ecosystem functions vital for life. The higher the biodiversity, the greater the ability of an ecosystem to withstand adversities and adapt to environmental changes, which in turn ensures productivity and system stability.\nEconomically, biodiversity provides essential resources such as food, livestock, forests, fish, and medicinal resources. Crop and agro-biodiversity are crucial for food security and survival.\nScientifically, biodiversity gives us clues about the evolution of life, the functioning of ecosystems, and the importance of every species. It embodies our ethical responsibility to respect all life forms, contributing to sustainable human culture and development. The conservation of biodiversity ensures balance and supports human existence.\n(ii) What are the major factors that are responsible for the loss of biodiversity? What steps are needed to prevent them?\nAnswer:\nThe main factors responsible for the loss of biodiversity include human population growth, over-exploitation of resources, deforestation, destruction of habitats, pollution, natural calamities, and the introduction of exotic species. Activities like poaching, use of pesticides, and habitat fragmentation also contribute to rapid species decline and endangerment.\nTo prevent biodiversity loss, steps required are: preserving endangered species, proper management and planning to avoid extinction, conservation of food crops and wild relatives, protection of wildlife habitats, regulation of international trade in wild species, and sustainable development practices involving local communities. Legal frameworks like the Wild Life (Protection) Act, establishment of national parks, sanctuaries, biosphere reserves, and global agreements like the Convention of Biodiversity help safeguard biodiversity. Public education and responsible use of natural resources are essential for long-term conservation.\nBiodiversity and Conservation NCERT Solutions 2026-27: Key Concepts\nMastering\nBiodiversity and Conservation\nis vital for scoring high in Geography. This chapter helps students understand the importance of preserving our natural resources and highlights why\necosystem diversity\nand protection are crucial for the planet's future.\nThe chapter explores\ngenetic diversity\n, species richness, and conservation strategies. Reviewing well-structured answers boosts your exam confidence and ensures you remember the\nmajor factors\naffecting biodiversity. Use these insights to strengthen your conceptual clarity.\nPractice all exercise questions regularly and revise key definitions. Understanding the causes and solutions for biodiversity loss will help you approach Geography questions smartly and achieve\nbetter results\nin your Board exams.\nCBSE Class 11 Geography Chapter-wise NCERT Solutions\nS.No\nChapter-wise NCERT Solutions for Geography Class 11\n1\nChapter 1 - Geography as a Discipline Solutions\n2\nChapter 2 - The Origin and Evolution of the Earth Solutions\n3\nChapter 3 - Interior of the Earth Solutions\n4\nChapter 4 - Distribution of Oceans and Continents Solutions\n5\nChapter 5 - Geomorphic Processes Solutions\n6\nChapter 6 - Landforms and Their Evolution Solutions\n7\nChapter 7 - Composition and Structure of Atmosphere Solutions\n8\nChapter 8 - Solar Radiation Heat Balance and Temperature Solutions\n9\nChapter 9 - Atmospheric Circulation and Weather Systems Solutions\n10\nChapter 10 - Water in the Atmosphere Solutions\n11\nChapter 11 - World Climate and Climate Change Solutions\n12\nChapter 12 - Water Oceans Solutions\n13\nChapter 13 - Movements of Ocean Water Solutions\nCBSE Class 11 Geography Study Materials\nS.No\nStudy Materials for Class 11 Geography\n1\nCBSE Class 11 Geography NCERT Solutions\n2\nCBSE Class 11 Geography NCERT Book"
